WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.770
- [Host] Warsaw, Poland, is
home to some delicious dishes:

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.540
like schabowy-mmm pretty good;

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.710
pierogi-mmm, yeah;

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.500
and, ooh, one sec, yes, and this-

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.343
pig's feet in jelly.

00:00:15.787 --> 00:00:18.313
Look at the way it's
wobbling, it just wobbles.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.110
This is nóżki w galarecie.

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:26.840
Translated to English, it
means pig's feet in jelly.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.173
Yes, that's a pig's foot in jelly.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.360
This traditional Polish
dish has been served

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.902
for over a hundred years.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.700
Barbara has been whipping up the dish

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.810
for family occasions for decades.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:43.080
That's because she thinks pig
feet in jelly is, well ...

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:02.050
- [Host] Thanks, Barbara!

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.040
It's claimed that the
first meat jelly dishes

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.600
were served in 1518 at a wedding feast

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.670
of an old Polish king and queen.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.320
Back then, pork wasn't so popular,

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.380
so it was served with
either young chickens

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.910
or even fish.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:20.370
Here in central Warsaw, it's on the menu.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:23.063
Marek is the head chef; he
knows the recipe by heart.

00:01:59.191 --> 00:02:00.234
- [Host] Ooh, vodka!

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:03.651
OK, but what's the deal with the jelly?

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:21.230
- [Host] So it's the
proteins from the bones?

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:25.833
- [Host] Ehh, and now
the most important part:

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:28.571
the taste.

00:02:28.571 --> 00:02:31.821
(classical music)

00:02:31.821 --> 00:02:36.385
Mmm, mm, mm, mm, mmm pretty good.

00:02:36.385 --> 00:02:40.302
(classical instrumental music)

